[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: L2 — Configuration
UID: QMGMT-L2C
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: RST
  AUTO_LEVELS: On

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Command execution

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-EXEC-010
TITLE: Command execution in qube
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall run a caller-supplied command inside a qube and
return that command's exit status.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OPERATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-EXEC-020
TITLE: File transfer
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall transfer a file between the qube it is running in and the one being managed.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OPERATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-EXEC-030
TITLE: Execution user selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall run a command in a qube under a caller-specified user
account.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt, QubesTools
RATIONALE: >>>
Running as root where the unprivileged user suffices widens the blast radius of
a compromised or malicious guest command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-OPERATE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Management isolation

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-SEC-020
TITLE: Management qube isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall carry out a target's configuration work inside a
disposable qube dedicated to that target.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
A disposable qube shared between targets would let one managed qube observe or
influence the configuration of another.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_create

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-SEC-030
TITLE: Management policy lifetime
STATEMENT: >>>
When a management run over a target ends, the management tool shall revoke the administrative policy granted for that target for any ephemeral management qubes created in the process.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-SEC-040
TITLE: Output sanitisation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall sanitise text received from a managed qube before
writing it to a dom0 terminal.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
Terminal escape sequences in qube-supplied output are an injection path into
the administrator's dom0 session.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-SEC-050
TITLE: Disposable qube bypass prevention
STATEMENT: >>>
If a run is configured to bypass the management disposable qube, then the
management tool shall refuse to start that run.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Unwanted-behaviour
PRODUCT: Ansible, Salt
RATIONALE: >>>
The isolation boundary is only worth anything if it cannot be turned off by a
configuration setting the administrator may not have reviewed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Delegation

[PRODUCT_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L2C-DELEG-010
TITLE: Configuration delegation
STATEMENT: >>>
The management tool shall hand a provisioned qube to a configuration management tool to configure
that qube's contents.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Terraform
RATIONALE: >>>
Delegation is achieved by invoking operations inside the qube, as its L3s show.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-RECONCILE
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ADMINAPI
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L1-ISOLATION
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]
